cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these kernels, cite the engine whose animation semantics they restate.
title: Bone kernels (Lean-emitted)
abstract: >-
  lean/Bone/SlangCodegen/*.lean restate the per-frame work of the engine's clip
  player and skeleton as LeanSlang compute kernels on the drape kernels' layout
  (a params block at binding 0, flat buffers): keyframe sampling with the
  engine's Animation track samplers: all interpolation modes, loop modes,
  transitions and backward nearest keys (bone_sample, with Curves.lean), the
  mixer's per-bone blend of several instances with filter weights,
  deterministic or normalised weighting and Animation::interpolate_via_rest
  (bone_blend), the root-motion arms of _blend_process and _blend_apply
  (root_motion), the
  local pose matrix with Basis::set_quaternion_scale (bone_local), the
  skeleton-space pose by pointer jumping over the parent links, one round per
  dispatch and ceil(log2(depth + 1)) rounds for any tree shape (bone_jump), and
  the bind-pose product in the skeleton buffer's 3x4 row layout (bone_skin).
  lake exe emit_bone writes them as Slang into slang/, and gen.sh compiles them
  to cpp/ (servers) and spv/ (GPU clients). No engine source is copied.
  Verified against the engine's own CPU clip player and skeleton by
  tests/bone_kernels (C++ emission; fan, chain and random-parent fixtures) and
  by GPU runs of the bytecode on the engine's local rendering device.
type: software
authors:
  - name: K. S. Ernest (iFire) Lee
  - name: V-Sekai
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/contract-bone-kernels
license: MIT
